<DemoExample Title="Style & Class" RazorCode="@example24RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example24CsharpCode" Id="example24">
    <div>Customizes the appearance at every level: Style and Class on the root element, per-item styles and classes, and the Styles and Classes objects that target the internal parts of the component, including the checked state of the items.</div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Component's Style & Class:</div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-content column">
        <BitChoiceGroup Label="Styled ChoiceGroup"
                        Items="basicItems"
                        DefaultValue="basicItems[1].Value"
                        Style="margin-inline: 16px; color:lightseagreen; text-shadow: lightseagreen 0 0 8px;" />

        <BitChoiceGroup Label="Classed ChoiceGroup"
                        Items="basicItems"
                        DefaultValue="basicItems[1].Value"
                        Class="custom-class" />
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br /><br />
    <div>Item's Style & Class:</div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-content column">
        <BitChoiceGroup Items="itemStyleClassItems" DefaultValue="itemStyleClassItems[1].Value" />
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br /><br />
    <div><b>Styles</b> & <b>Classes</b>:</div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-content column">
        <BitChoiceGroup Label="Styles"
                        Items="basicItems"
                        DefaultValue="basicItems[1].Value"
                        Styles="@(new() { Root = "margin-inline: 16px; --item-background: #d3d3d347; --item-border: 1px solid gray;",
                                          ItemLabel = "width: 100%; cursor: pointer;",
                                          ItemChecked = "--item-background: #87cefa24; --item-border: 1px solid dodgerblue;",
                                          ItemContainer = "padding: 8px; border-radius: 2px; background-color: var(--item-background); border: var(--item-border);" })" />

        <BitChoiceGroup Label="Classes"
                        Items="basicItems"
                        DefaultValue="basicItems[1].Value"
                        Classes="@(new() { Root = "custom-root",
                                           ItemText = "custom-text",
                                           ItemChecked = "custom-checked",
                                           ItemRadioButton = "custom-radio-btn" })" />
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br /><br />
    <div><b>CSS variables</b>:</div>
    <br />
    <div>
        The ChoiceGroup also reads a set of <BitLink Href="#css-variables-section">CSS variables</BitLink> off its root for what no
        parameter covers. They inherit, so a value on <code>:root</code> or any ancestor re-skins every ChoiceGroup below it, and one
        on the <b>Style</b> of an instance re-skins that one alone.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-content column">
        <BitChoiceGroup Label="Bigger circle, square focus ring, wider gap"
                        Items="basicItems"
                        DefaultValue="@("A")"
                        Style="--bit-ChoiceGroup-circle-size: 1.5rem; --bit-ChoiceGroup-dot-size: 0.75rem; --bit-ChoiceGroup-gap: 1rem; --bit-ChoiceGroup-item-radius: 0;" />

        <BitChoiceGroup Label="Recolored, and without the bold checked text"
                        Items="basicItems"
                        DefaultValue="@("B")"
                        Style="--bit-ChoiceGroup-color: rebeccapurple; --bit-ChoiceGroup-hover-color: mediumpurple; --bit-ChoiceGroup-circle-color: mediumpurple; --bit-ChoiceGroup-circle-hover-color: rebeccapurple; --bit-ChoiceGroup-item-checked-font-weight: 400;" />
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>Set once on an ancestor, inherited by every ChoiceGroup inside it:</div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-content" style="--bit-ChoiceGroup-color: seagreen; --bit-ChoiceGroup-item-checked-background: #2e8b5724; --bit-ChoiceGroup-item-border-color: #2e8b5766;">
        <BitChoiceGroup Label="Outline" Variant="BitVariant.Outline" Items="basicItems" DefaultValue="@("A")" />
        <BitChoiceGroup Label="Fill" Variant="BitVariant.Fill" Items="basicItems" DefaultValue="@("B")" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="RTL" RazorCode="@example25RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example25CsharpCode" Id="example25" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>Renders the ChoiceGroup in right-to-left mode; the layout is mirrored, and the arrow keys follow the text direction in Chromium and Firefox, where ArrowLeft moves to the next item. That mirroring is the native behavior of a radio group in those engines rather than something the component does, and WebKit does not do it: there the arrows keep the order of the markup, so ArrowRight moves to the next item and ArrowLeft to the previous one.</div>
    <br />
    <div dir="rtl" class="example-content">
        <BitChoiceGroup Label="ساده" Items="rtlItems" DefaultValue="@("A")" Dir="BitDir.Rtl" />
        <BitChoiceGroup Label="غیرفعال" Items="rtlItems" IsEnabled="false" DefaultValue="@("A")" Dir="BitDir.Rtl" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

